title: PoV size reclaim fix
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |
    This PR introduces incremental storage root estimation for PoV reclaim, addressing
    issue #6020. Storage weight reclaim allows parachains to return unused PoV space
    from completed extrinsics, but previously didn't account for storage root calculation.

    When items are written or deleted during extrinsic execution, they're only noted in
    the overlay. However, when calculating the storage root at block finalization, trie
    nodes must be accessed to insert/delete/merge the changes. These trie node accesses
    are recorded in the proof, causing the actual PoV size to exceed estimates.

    The solution introduces incremental storage root estimation that approximates trie
    node accesses that would occur during storage root calculation, without actually
    computing the root hash. This is triggered after each extrinsic via the weight reclaim
    pallet using a new version 2 of the storage_proof_size host function.

    The estimation also needs two state-machine fixes for runtimes that compute a storage
    root or a child root in the middle of a block. Both change what such runtimes observe,
    so they come as new host function versions and the existing versions keep their exact
    behaviour:
    - storage::append version 2 drops a storage root cached by an earlier storage::root.
      Version 1 keeps it, so the block's root and storage transaction can miss the append.
    - default_child_storage::root version 3 never writes the child root into the main
      storage overlay and does not return a stale root after a mid-block storage::root.
      Version 2 does both.
    - storage_proof_size version 2 adds the estimation.

    The bodies of the old and the new versions are separate, callable items:
    Externalities::storage_append and storage_append_v2,
    Externalities::child_storage_root_with_version and child_storage_root_v3, and
    storage_proof_size_v1 and storage_proof_size_v2 in
    cumulus-primitives-proof-size-hostfunction.

    All three new versions are registered only: nodes provide them, but runtimes keep
    calling the old versions, and the validate_block shims in
    cumulus-pallet-parachain-system keep answering the old versions. Nothing changes for
    runtimes until the markers are dropped. The three markers must be dropped together, in
    the same release that switches the three shims (host_storage_append,
    host_default_child_storage_root, host_storage_proof_size) to the new bodies: the
    estimation is only sound with the child root semantics of version 3.
